WEBVTT

00:01.001 --> 00:04.587
♪ <i>It seems today that all you see</i> ♪

00:04.588 --> 00:08.174
♪ <i>Is violence in movies and sex on TV</i> ♪

00:08.175 --> 00:11.511
♪ <i>But where are those
good old-fashioned values</i> ♪

00:11.512 --> 00:14.472
♪ <i>On which we used to rely?</i> ♪

00:14.473 --> 00:18.184
♪ <i>Lucky there's a family guy</i> ♪

00:18.185 --> 00:21.604
♪ <i>Lucky there's a man who
positively can do</i> ♪

00:21.605 --> 00:23.189
♪ <i>All the things that make us</i> ♪

00:23.190 --> 00:24.690
♪ <i>Laugh and cry</i> ♪

00:24.691 --> 00:30.155
♪ <i>He's... a... Fam... ily... Guy!</i> ♪

00:37.454 --> 00:40.540
God, the Clam sucks
on Saturday mornings.

00:40.541 --> 00:43.042
It's all just weird foreign sports fans,

00:43.043 --> 00:45.795
like those Pakistani cricket hooligans.

00:45.796 --> 00:47.547
If you are not rooting for Lahore,

00:47.548 --> 00:49.423
please you may leave, I can tell you!

00:49.424 --> 00:51.384
Lahore cricketers are the best,

00:51.385 --> 00:54.095
and the others are <i>not</i> the best,
dear friends.

00:54.096 --> 00:58.307
I'm for Karachi, but I don't
got a death wish about it.

00:58.308 --> 01:00.226
Guys, what's wrong with us?

01:00.227 --> 01:02.520
It's Saturday morning,
and we're drinking in a bar.

01:02.521 --> 01:05.064
We should be drinking at
the Goodwill donation dumpster.

01:05.065 --> 01:06.187
Why come?

01:06.188 --> 01:08.150
'Cause right now's when
all the yard sales end.

01:08.151 --> 01:10.486
We can get first pick
of the abandoned leftovers.

01:10.487 --> 01:12.196
That's a stupid idea. There's not gonna

01:12.197 --> 01:13.884
be anything good in that dumpster.

01:13.885 --> 01:16.995
What if I told you
everything I'm wearing right now

01:16.996 --> 01:18.494
I found in that dumpster?

01:19.706 --> 01:21.414
Is that a bachelorette sash?

01:21.415 --> 01:25.460
Scott said I could do hand stuff
this weekend, but that's it.

01:28.922 --> 01:30.590
I told you this is stupid.

01:30.591 --> 01:31.924
There's nothing good in here.

01:31.925 --> 01:33.718
Hey, look a pair of working legs.

01:33.719 --> 01:35.052
Dibs on these.

01:35.053 --> 01:37.305
Wha...? Aw, come on, Quagmire!

01:37.306 --> 01:38.931
Joe, I said dibs.

01:38.932 --> 01:41.309
No, no, you're right. You said dibs.

01:41.310 --> 01:44.353
Whoa. Check it out. A Sorry! board game.

01:44.354 --> 01:45.605
Let me see it.

01:47.232 --> 01:49.400
- Three pieces missing.
- How'd you do that?

01:49.401 --> 01:52.613
I can shake anything and
figure out what all's in there.

01:55.115 --> 01:57.825
You got 11 periods left.

01:57.826 --> 02:00.369
Cool. VHS of <i>Eraserhead.</i>

02:00.370 --> 02:03.372
This'll be good for when
I never want to sleep again.

02:03.373 --> 02:06.042
Holy crap.

02:06.043 --> 02:07.502
Wha-What? What is it?

02:10.422 --> 02:12.048
A Magic 8 Ball!

02:12.049 --> 02:13.966
This thing can tell the future.

02:13.967 --> 02:16.218
No, it can't, Peter.
It's just a stupid toy.

02:16.219 --> 02:17.720
I don't know. Let's test it.

02:17.721 --> 02:20.931
Will there be snow this Christmas?

02:20.932 --> 02:23.601
Oh, my God, the ball is right.

02:23.602 --> 02:25.227
I <i>should</i> ask again later.

02:25.228 --> 02:26.771
How did it know that?

02:26.772 --> 02:28.814
Guys, from now on, I am living my life

02:28.815 --> 02:30.900
according to the Magic 8 Ball.

02:30.901 --> 02:32.652
It will lead me like the shorebird

02:32.653 --> 02:35.197
that led the first Pilgrims to Boston.

02:36.156 --> 02:38.949
Ahoy! Are you looking to build a city

02:38.950 --> 02:41.911
where sports fans
can be notoriously racist?

02:41.912 --> 02:44.163
Yeah, and can we also ruin
"Sweet Caroline"

02:44.164 --> 02:46.707
- for everyone else?
- Absolutely.

02:46.708 --> 02:50.044
Can our airport security people
be responsible for 9/11?

02:50.045 --> 02:53.631
And can our own 9/11 be, like,
one one-thousandth as bad,

02:53.632 --> 02:55.841
but we'll still make
a fricking movie about it?

02:55.842 --> 02:57.635
I think I know just the place.

02:57.636 --> 03:00.221
Okay, I don't know
if this is gonna be a problem,

03:00.222 --> 03:02.223
but we forgot to bring the letter "R."

03:02.224 --> 03:03.849
No problem at all.

03:03.850 --> 03:06.227
Right this way, large-faced whites!

03:06.228 --> 03:08.229
Let's go, Red Sox!

03:09.648 --> 03:12.025
Let's go, Red Sox!

03:17.030 --> 03:18.656
What is that?

03:18.657 --> 03:20.199
It's my Magic 8 Ball.

03:20.200 --> 03:21.784
This is the first black ball

03:21.785 --> 03:23.994
that Kim Kardashian hasn't played with.

03:23.995 --> 03:26.956
Why is it filled with the blue
liquid from tampon commercials?

03:26.957 --> 03:28.499
That's a very gross question, Meg.

03:28.500 --> 03:30.840
You may take your breakfast
in the attic.

03:32.254 --> 03:35.297
That question aside, I'm having
a blast with my new 8 Ball.

03:35.298 --> 03:36.855
It knows everything. Watch.

03:36.856 --> 03:38.467
Magic 8 Ball,

03:38.468 --> 03:41.638
will my middle-of-the-highway
puppet show be a success?

03:43.196 --> 03:45.198
Well, I'll show this thing.

03:52.983 --> 03:54.389
How'd it go, Dad?

03:54.390 --> 03:56.410
I don't know, Sparky.
What did you think?

03:56.411 --> 03:59.363
The performance was a little flat.

04:14.296 --> 04:16.714
Magic 8 Ball.

04:16.715 --> 04:18.507
Magic 8 Ball, I'm bored.

04:18.508 --> 04:21.021
Should I sniff my coworker's hair?

04:23.805 --> 04:25.347
He told me to do it!

04:25.348 --> 04:27.391
Mr. Griffin, if a Magic 8 Ball asked you

04:27.392 --> 04:29.727
to jump off a building,
would you do that, too?

04:29.728 --> 04:31.061
Did it?

04:31.062 --> 04:33.606
No, I'm just using that
as an example of...

04:33.607 --> 04:35.650
I listened to the toy!

04:39.112 --> 04:42.532
Magic 8 Ball,
what's the best email provider?

04:44.117 --> 04:46.410
"Outlook good." Interesting.

04:46.411 --> 04:48.913
He's not raving about it,
but it's a solid choice.

04:48.914 --> 04:50.873
Let's go, Peter. Time for church.

04:50.874 --> 04:54.126
Mom said they're gonna serve
Chewy Chips Ahoy at coffee hour.

04:54.127 --> 04:55.795
Lois... church?

04:55.796 --> 04:57.797
Who am I supposed to worship, Jesus?

04:57.798 --> 04:59.632
<i>This</i> is my god now.

04:59.633 --> 05:01.091
Watch your mouth, Peter.

05:01.092 --> 05:03.886
Sorry, Lois, but my religion
is now the 8 Ball.

05:03.887 --> 05:07.056
Magic 8 Ball,
is the Fox network sustainable

05:07.057 --> 05:09.059
in this new streaming world?

05:10.018 --> 05:13.020
No. No!

05:14.606 --> 05:16.106
Kim, what's wrong?

05:16.107 --> 05:19.486
A black ball went to waste.

05:27.202 --> 05:29.370
Are you streaming <i>Mindhunter</i> in church?

05:29.371 --> 05:32.165
I'm <i>trying</i> to stream
<i>Mindhunter</i> in church.

05:36.253 --> 05:37.962
Freaking guest Wi-Fi.

05:37.963 --> 05:40.548
You know the priest gets the good Wi-Fi.

05:40.549 --> 05:42.299
And yea, the Lord said...

05:42.300 --> 05:44.134
Whoa, whoa. <i>Mindhunter's</i> going in.

05:44.135 --> 05:45.803
I mean...

05:45.804 --> 05:48.472
Thou art the children
of Abraham, and thou shalt...

05:48.473 --> 05:50.015
He's playing you!

05:50.016 --> 05:52.101
You think you're playing him?
He's playing you.

05:52.102 --> 05:54.270
I hate this. When do I get my cookie?

05:54.271 --> 05:56.438
I just want my cookie so I can go home.

05:56.439 --> 05:58.649
Now please join me in silent prayer.

05:58.650 --> 06:00.526
And as we settle into the silence,

06:00.527 --> 06:02.778
I remind you that... in honor of Lent...

06:02.779 --> 06:07.242
today's coffee service will not
include Chewy Chips Ahoy.

06:11.454 --> 06:13.331
(BLEEP)

06:18.169 --> 06:20.838
Hey, Stewie said his first word.

06:20.839 --> 06:23.048
And it was a swear.

06:23.049 --> 06:25.134
Well, this is unacceptable.

06:25.135 --> 06:27.678
We have to leave right now
and go straight to breakfast.

06:27.679 --> 06:29.848
Unbelievable.

06:34.728 --> 06:36.938
Let's go!

06:42.777 --> 06:45.738
I can't believe Stewie
finally said his first word

06:45.739 --> 06:48.073
and it ends up being... that.

06:48.074 --> 06:51.201
Right now, every woman in my
mommy wine group is judging me.

06:51.202 --> 06:53.996
I may have to start
drinking wine at home alone.

06:53.997 --> 06:55.994
- Start?
- Not the day for it, Chris!

06:55.995 --> 06:57.166
Not the day!

06:57.167 --> 06:59.418
I don't get it, Stewie.
You've been talking forever.

06:59.419 --> 07:01.045
Why did everyone suddenly
understand you now?

07:01.046 --> 07:02.713
I don't know.

07:02.714 --> 07:05.049
I was feeling so much
intense emotion in the moment,

07:05.050 --> 07:07.343
and that one word somehow
just burst through.

07:07.344 --> 07:09.637
Yeah, but now what?
Everyone can understand you?

07:09.638 --> 07:11.347
I don't think so.

07:11.348 --> 07:13.933
Not unless I'm yelling something
I feel strongly about.

07:13.934 --> 07:17.019
Greta Gerwig is a national treasure!

07:17.020 --> 07:18.687
See? Nothing.

07:18.688 --> 07:20.564
I guess I'm not feeling it.
I don't know.

07:20.565 --> 07:23.567
What if that's the only thing
I'll ever be able to express?

07:23.568 --> 07:26.320
Anger. What kind
of a person would I be then?

07:26.321 --> 07:28.030
Larry David, Lewis Black,

07:28.031 --> 07:30.282
a Trump voter, everyone on Twitter.

07:30.283 --> 07:32.326
But I don't want
to be any of those things.

07:32.327 --> 07:33.702
They've got to hear me.

07:33.703 --> 07:35.621
Ice cream! Lollipop!

07:35.622 --> 07:37.039
Bubbles! Kitty cat!

07:38.458 --> 07:40.459
Doggy! Raincoat! Preschool!

07:40.460 --> 07:44.421
Fire truck! Goldfish! Finger paint!

07:48.802 --> 07:50.386
Lois, what are you doing here?

07:50.387 --> 07:52.513
What do you mean? You invited us.

07:52.514 --> 07:55.391
Sorry, but we can't have Stewie here.

07:55.392 --> 07:56.976
I brought my own veggie burgers,

07:56.977 --> 07:58.602
but I'm not gonna make
a big deal about it.

07:58.603 --> 08:00.854
What with his profanity and all,
I don't think

08:00.855 --> 08:03.357
Stewie would be a good influence
on the other children.

08:03.358 --> 08:05.192
Is there a designated spot on the grill

08:05.193 --> 08:06.568
for the veggie burgers?

08:06.569 --> 08:08.070
And again, not a big deal.

08:08.071 --> 08:10.197
You're saying
that because of a swear word,

08:10.198 --> 08:12.950
my son isn't good enough
for your pool party?

08:12.951 --> 08:14.743
It's a little bit about him swearing,

08:14.744 --> 08:17.288
but mostly about <i>you</i> as a parent.

08:18.498 --> 08:20.416
Kevin, I said, no arrows!

08:20.417 --> 08:22.251
Crossbows don't shoot arrows.

08:22.252 --> 08:24.044
They shoot bolts, dumb-ass!

08:24.045 --> 08:26.088
Okay, sweetie.

08:26.089 --> 08:29.466
Hey, Dad,
did you hear what Einstein called bolts?

08:29.467 --> 08:31.052
I heard it.

08:34.472 --> 08:36.223
Brian, shut off the television.

08:36.224 --> 08:37.933
It's ruined my baby!

08:37.934 --> 08:39.351
What are you talking about?

08:39.352 --> 08:41.895
Stewie obviously learned
to swear from some TV show.

08:41.896 --> 08:44.606
No, he didn't. The only show
he watches is <i>Caillou.</i>

08:44.607 --> 08:46.734
Well, then that little
French-Canadian weirdo

08:46.735 --> 08:48.819
is the potty mouth, I'm sure of it.

08:48.820 --> 08:51.613
And I'm willing to watch every
single episode just to prove it.

08:51.614 --> 08:53.490
<i>Caillou was upset.</i>

08:53.491 --> 08:57.036
<i>Why am I bald? I'm not a baby. I'm four.</i>

08:57.037 --> 08:59.538
<i>Are kids just bald in Canada?</i>

08:59.539 --> 09:01.081
<i>So Caillou decided</i>

09:01.082 --> 09:02.624
<i>to look himself up on Wikipedia.</i>

09:02.625 --> 09:04.668
God, this is dull.

09:04.669 --> 09:06.920
<i>Maybe I'm supposed
to be a cancer survivor,</i>

09:06.921 --> 09:09.423
<i>and this show is very inspiring.</i>

09:09.424 --> 09:11.925
<i>But Caillou wasn't a cancer survivor.</i>

09:11.926 --> 09:15.387
<i>The show's creators
just made a weird choice.</i>

09:15.388 --> 09:17.931
<i>Caillou's low-testosterone father</i>

09:17.932 --> 09:20.434
<i>again indulged Caillou's tantrum,</i>

09:20.435 --> 09:22.770
<i>clearly trying to raise a sociopath.</i>

09:22.771 --> 09:24.354
<i>It's okay, Caillou.</i>

09:24.355 --> 09:26.315
<i>I'll bake you a pie.</i>

09:26.316 --> 09:28.901
<i>He said,
his body flooding with estrogen.</i>

09:28.902 --> 09:30.319
Lois?

09:30.320 --> 09:31.820
Are you dead?

09:33.198 --> 09:34.865
Can I eat you?

09:34.866 --> 09:36.992
- Huh? What?
- Ah, another time.

09:36.993 --> 09:41.205
Oh. I-I, um... I watched
that <i>Caillou,</i> and you're right.

09:41.206 --> 09:43.540
Stewie didn't learn that word
from <i>Caillou.</i>

09:43.541 --> 09:45.626
That means he learned it
from someone in this house.

09:45.627 --> 09:48.003
- Okay.
- And I will find out who.

09:48.004 --> 09:49.630
I'm gonna set a trap

09:49.631 --> 09:52.174
and lure the swearer
into revealing himself.

09:52.175 --> 09:53.550
That sounds hard.

09:53.551 --> 09:56.178
Oh, I <i>will</i> find the swearer.

09:56.179 --> 09:57.596
<i>Dad, why are we sitting</i>

09:57.597 --> 09:59.098
<i>on the washing machine?</i>

09:59.099 --> 10:00.516
<i>Because in Canada,</i>

10:00.517 --> 10:02.477
<i>men have vaginas.</i>

10:06.564 --> 10:09.108
Hey, what's with the stairs?
Why do they look different?

10:09.109 --> 10:10.609
Oh, I'm trying to prove

10:10.610 --> 10:12.778
that Peter's the one
cussing in the house,

10:12.779 --> 10:15.447
so I waxed the staircase
for him to fall down.

10:15.448 --> 10:17.616
Hey, Lois,
have you seen my Spider-Man socks?

10:17.617 --> 10:18.784
I can't seem to...

10:18.785 --> 10:20.410
Ouch. Oh, heavens.

10:20.411 --> 10:21.787
Oh, goodness gracious.

10:21.788 --> 10:23.664
That's smarts. Oh, my.

10:23.665 --> 10:25.249
Egad. Well, I'll be.

10:25.250 --> 10:27.251
Yikes.

10:27.252 --> 10:29.128
Peter, when did you become so polite?

10:29.129 --> 10:31.338
Oh, I've been hanging out
with Caillou's beta dad.

10:31.339 --> 10:33.298
In fact, I'm meeting him at the park

10:33.299 --> 10:35.802
to eat unsalted saltines on the swings.

10:36.845 --> 10:38.095
I feel like you're wearing

10:38.096 --> 10:41.683
what Rachel Maddow
would wear to a pumpkin patch.

10:44.102 --> 10:46.019
<i>Lois couldn't find the swearer,</i>

10:46.020 --> 10:47.855
<i>nor could she remove the voice</i>

10:47.856 --> 10:50.858
<i>of the grating</i> Caillou <i>narrator</i>
<i>from her head.</i>

10:50.859 --> 10:52.818
Make it stop!

10:52.819 --> 10:55.196
<i>Not until you kill them all, Lois.</i>

10:56.156 --> 10:57.531
Oh, crap.

10:57.532 --> 10:59.491
It's the lady with the baby who cussed.

10:59.492 --> 11:01.243
Turn out the lights.

11:01.244 --> 11:02.578
Shh. Quiet, quiet.

11:02.579 --> 11:04.496
H-Hello?

11:04.497 --> 11:06.748
Hello! I know you're in there!

11:06.749 --> 11:08.333
We're closed!

11:08.334 --> 11:10.627
I know you're not closed.

11:10.628 --> 11:12.462
I see the Instacart people in there

11:12.463 --> 11:14.631
emotionlessly filling up their baskets.

11:14.632 --> 11:16.133
We're a family establishment,

11:16.134 --> 11:18.260
so take your foul-mouthed baby
and go away!

11:18.261 --> 11:20.095
Please, let me in!

11:20.096 --> 11:22.681
I can only poop
behind a punch-code door!

11:22.682 --> 11:23.932
There's something about the beeps.

11:23.933 --> 11:25.350
It gets things moving!

11:25.351 --> 11:27.102
It's very secure!

11:27.103 --> 11:28.604
Go away!

11:28.605 --> 11:30.522
You can't do this!

11:30.523 --> 11:32.774
When a mom is shunned by groceries,

11:32.775 --> 11:35.944
she has nothing!

11:35.945 --> 11:39.157
Please!

11:40.992 --> 11:45.162
Aah! It's those antibacterial
wipes for the shopping carts!

11:45.163 --> 11:46.914
It's burning my eyes!

11:46.915 --> 11:49.334
(BLEEP)!

11:52.837 --> 11:53.879
Oh, my God.

11:53.880 --> 11:55.547
I-It's me.

11:55.548 --> 11:57.341
I'm the swearer.

11:57.342 --> 12:00.260
Oh, God.

12:00.261 --> 12:03.597
I'm ruining my child!

12:03.598 --> 12:05.057
<i>Lois was sad,</i>

12:05.058 --> 12:07.309
<i>but not as sad as she was going to be</i>

12:07.310 --> 12:10.312
<i>when she realizes she has
to use those ouchie wipes</i>

12:10.313 --> 12:13.858
<i>to make a potty next
to the store dumpster.</i>

12:18.863 --> 12:21.156
I feel so awful.

12:21.157 --> 12:22.699
I've corrupted my baby

12:22.700 --> 12:25.827
with my foul language
and my terrible anger.

12:25.828 --> 12:28.038
I'm so sorry that happened, Lois.

12:28.039 --> 12:30.415
And Lofthouse cookies weren't available

12:30.416 --> 12:31.917
at any other grocery store?

12:31.918 --> 12:34.419
Don't worry, Dad. I Instacarted some.

12:37.131 --> 12:38.298
Here's your stuff.

12:38.299 --> 12:39.466
Thank you. Have a good night.

12:39.467 --> 12:41.385
No.

12:41.386 --> 12:42.886
Anyway, the point is

12:42.887 --> 12:45.806
I have to deal with my anger
and fix myself.

12:45.807 --> 12:48.267
So I've decided to attend
this relaxation retreat

12:48.268 --> 12:50.894
at Vista del Vista Resort.

12:50.895 --> 12:52.479
Uh, gosh, I don't know about that, Lois.

12:52.480 --> 12:53.730
It sounds really expensive.

12:53.731 --> 12:55.983
No, I guess you're right.

12:55.984 --> 12:57.818
There's no way we can afford it.

12:57.819 --> 12:59.945
Plus, if I go,
that means I won't be here

12:59.946 --> 13:02.281
to help out around the house
or feed you guys

13:02.282 --> 13:04.950
or monitor your Internet usage
every day...

13:04.951 --> 13:05.951
- You should go.
- Yeah, Mom,

13:05.952 --> 13:07.577
you should go, for sure.

13:11.332 --> 13:14.085
Because they want to masturbate,
you see.

13:15.128 --> 13:16.333
Okay.

13:16.334 --> 13:17.995
Uh, I don't know what that was,

13:17.996 --> 13:19.464
but, Lois, you should go to that resort.

13:19.465 --> 13:21.216
Go relax and fix yourself.

13:21.217 --> 13:22.634
Really?

13:22.635 --> 13:24.469
You guys'll be okay while I'm gone?

13:24.470 --> 13:25.804
Sure. We'll have fun!

13:25.805 --> 13:28.515
Just like that time me and Chris
went Jet Ski'ing.

13:28.516 --> 13:30.600
Yeah! This is awesome!

13:30.601 --> 13:31.810
I know, right?

13:33.229 --> 13:34.271
Oh, my God!

13:34.272 --> 13:35.272
It's okay, Chris.

13:35.273 --> 13:36.481
I'm sure that was the only one.

13:36.482 --> 13:38.108
Dolphins swim alone.

13:41.779 --> 13:44.031
Okay, maybe we should turn back.

13:44.032 --> 13:45.282
No.

13:45.283 --> 13:48.243
Kill every last one of them.

13:48.244 --> 13:50.537
<i>Chris and I never spoke of that day.</i>

13:50.538 --> 13:53.999
<i>But whenever somebody talks
about how smart dolphins are,</i>

13:54.000 --> 13:55.792
<i>Chris and I look at each other like,</i>

13:55.793 --> 13:57.669
<i>"No."</i>

14:00.631 --> 14:04.968
♪ <i>You got to ac-cent-tchu-ate</i>
<i>the positive</i> ♪

14:04.969 --> 14:08.847
♪ <i>E-lim-I-nate the negative</i> ♪

14:08.848 --> 14:10.932
♪ <i>And latch on</i> ♪

14:10.933 --> 14:13.602
♪ <i>To the affirmative.</i> ♪

14:13.603 --> 14:16.063
Lois Griffin? My name is Roger,

14:16.064 --> 14:18.315
and I'll be guiding
this relaxation adventure

14:18.316 --> 14:20.067
for you and the other white women,

14:20.068 --> 14:22.611
plus an Asian woman who has
a white husband back home.

14:22.612 --> 14:25.197
I feel more relaxed already.

14:25.198 --> 14:28.867
Now sit down and enjoy some
spa music that's mostly rain.

14:28.868 --> 14:31.829
Hey, guys, can we take it
from the rain again?

14:42.215 --> 14:43.882
Well, Chris and Meg are off to school.

14:43.883 --> 14:45.467
Guess it's just you and me now.

14:45.468 --> 14:46.802
You want a Popsicle?

14:46.803 --> 14:47.803
Huh?

14:47.804 --> 14:49.972
Breakfast Popsicle?

14:51.057 --> 14:53.058
Whoa, there's vodka in here.

14:57.063 --> 14:58.814
Now, what... Uh, now, what is...

14:58.815 --> 15:00.565
Now, what... what did you want?

15:00.566 --> 15:01.650
What...

15:01.651 --> 15:03.485
Let's go play in the hot yard.

15:03.486 --> 15:05.862
I'm two and a half hours late
for preschool.

15:05.863 --> 15:06.863
Your dad...

15:06.864 --> 15:08.281
What... Who wants milk?

15:08.282 --> 15:10.784
L-Let me quick just check
in the freezer.

15:13.121 --> 15:15.455
You-you burger.

15:15.456 --> 15:17.290
Here-Here's your veggie burger.

15:18.709 --> 15:19.876
It'll thaw out.

15:19.877 --> 15:21.378
It... You s-suck on it.

15:21.379 --> 15:22.963
It'll thaw out nice.

15:22.964 --> 15:24.589
All right, I'm out of here.

15:24.590 --> 15:26.842
Ah, this is the perfect amount of drunk

15:26.843 --> 15:29.761
for a Filet-O-Fish.

15:33.683 --> 15:34.891
Hey.

15:34.892 --> 15:37.269
I'm, um, Trey Headband,

15:37.270 --> 15:40.439
and I'm your dumb yoga instructor?

15:40.440 --> 15:42.941
Yoga is, um, good?

15:42.942 --> 15:45.735
And from, um, like, China?

15:45.736 --> 15:47.779
Ready? Go.

15:47.780 --> 15:49.114
Go what?

15:49.115 --> 15:50.115
What?

15:50.116 --> 15:52.242
Y-You didn't tell us what to do.

15:52.243 --> 15:54.911
Awesome. You guys did great.

15:54.912 --> 15:56.329
Let's take a break.

15:56.330 --> 15:57.831
Who's got yoga questions?

15:57.832 --> 15:59.207
Oh, I have a question.

15:59.208 --> 16:01.293
What does "namaste" mean?

16:01.294 --> 16:02.377
I don't know.

16:02.378 --> 16:04.337
I've never heard of that.

16:04.338 --> 16:07.132
But do you guys remember OP shorts?

16:07.133 --> 16:09.509
- What does that have to do with yoga?
- I don't know.

16:09.510 --> 16:12.429
I'm just saying, those were pretty rad.

16:12.430 --> 16:15.432
You guys are doing really good.

16:15.433 --> 16:16.975
Keep going.

16:16.976 --> 16:19.186
I'm gonna go
to that bathroom right there

16:19.187 --> 16:21.606
and do explosive diarrhea.

16:22.982 --> 16:25.817
Just be quiet and meditate now.

16:25.818 --> 16:26.902
Right on?

16:30.156 --> 16:32.991
Just, like, be one with the silence.

16:36.996 --> 16:38.663
If you hear a sound,

16:38.664 --> 16:41.249
just, um, rec-knowledge it

16:41.250 --> 16:43.418
and then, like, let it go?

16:47.298 --> 16:50.634
Meditation doesn't have diarrhea sounds.

16:50.635 --> 16:53.554
All right, let's check in
on Peter and the baby.

16:54.847 --> 16:58.517
Okay, Stewie, time for Daddy
to mow this very rocky backyard.

16:58.518 --> 17:01.269
So I'll just put you in this
baby seat you've grown out of,

17:01.270 --> 17:02.604
right where the rocks are gonna fly.

17:02.605 --> 17:03.898
Wait, what?

17:06.651 --> 17:08.276
Hang on! Stop!

17:08.277 --> 17:10.445
- Aah!
- Uhp, there we go.

17:10.446 --> 17:13.114
Wow, that's a lot of rocks.

17:13.115 --> 17:14.908
Damn it! Ow! Ow! Turn it off!

17:14.909 --> 17:16.451
Uhp, the voles are back.

17:16.452 --> 17:18.912
You can tell
from all the very many rocks.

17:18.913 --> 17:20.288
Look at 'em fly!

17:21.666 --> 17:24.334
Still think moving was such a bad idea?

17:24.335 --> 17:25.335
I don't know.

17:25.336 --> 17:27.170
Do we still live with your mother?

17:41.060 --> 17:42.644
Good morning, everyone.

17:42.645 --> 17:44.896
Let me start
with another friendly reminder

17:44.897 --> 17:47.065
to please not flush
your feminine products.

17:47.066 --> 17:48.984
The yard over the septic tank out back

17:48.985 --> 17:51.194
looks like a <i>Braveheart</i> battlefield.

17:51.195 --> 17:54.739
Okay. Now it's time for everyone
to choose a mantra.

17:54.740 --> 17:55.812
What's that?

17:55.813 --> 17:58.159
It's like a word you say
that brings you peace.

17:58.160 --> 17:59.494
A special word.

17:59.495 --> 18:01.997
A word of release and catharsis.

18:01.998 --> 18:03.748
You mean like (BLEEP)?

18:05.084 --> 18:07.502
Now, now, Lois,
let's keep things acceptable.

18:07.503 --> 18:09.504
I mean, I'm just saying...
I already have a word

18:09.505 --> 18:11.339
that does all those things
when I say it.

18:11.340 --> 18:12.674
And that word is...

18:12.675 --> 18:14.467
Yes, we heard the word! Lois, please...

18:14.468 --> 18:16.136
No, no, maybe I'm not perfect,

18:16.137 --> 18:17.721
but I'm a good person.

18:17.722 --> 18:19.014
I love my children.

18:19.015 --> 18:20.140
I like my husband.

18:20.141 --> 18:21.224
And there are worse things

18:21.225 --> 18:23.560
than occasionally using a swear word.

18:23.561 --> 18:25.563
I'm out of here.

18:29.483 --> 18:31.568
Guys, I'm worried about the baby.

18:31.569 --> 18:33.778
He's hardly touched any of his birdseed.

18:33.779 --> 18:35.822
Are you sure we're shaking him enough?

18:35.823 --> 18:37.949
I'm home!

18:37.950 --> 18:39.868
Yeah!

18:39.869 --> 18:41.870
I missed you guys so much.

18:41.871 --> 18:43.872
I'm so sorry I had that little meltdown.

18:43.873 --> 18:44.956
But, more than that,

18:44.957 --> 18:47.292
I'm sorry I left you guys on your own.

18:47.293 --> 18:49.085
This is where I want to be.

18:49.086 --> 18:50.879
Is that okay with you guys?

18:50.880 --> 18:51.921
Of course, Lois.

18:51.922 --> 18:53.423
Everyone's glad you're home,

18:53.424 --> 18:55.592
except for mean older brother Buzz,

18:55.593 --> 18:57.218
who never says anything nice.

18:57.219 --> 18:58.928
Uh-oh. Here he is now.

18:58.929 --> 19:00.263
Hey, Lois.

19:00.264 --> 19:02.432
Pretty cool you're back.

19:02.433 --> 19:04.851
Aw, I guess he's not such
a bad guy after all.

19:04.852 --> 19:07.354
Also, America should only accept
white immigrants.

19:07.355 --> 19:09.564
Uhp, nope, he's still a bad guy.

19:09.565 --> 19:11.566
Well, I am so happy to be home.

19:11.567 --> 19:15.195
But there's one little guy
I missed most of all.

19:15.196 --> 19:18.114
Where's my baby?

19:24.372 --> 19:25.789
Stewie,

19:25.790 --> 19:27.457
I-it's me.

19:27.458 --> 19:29.376
I'm home.

19:31.962 --> 19:33.630
Mommy!

19:33.631 --> 19:35.632
Wow.

19:35.633 --> 19:37.258
It's Stewie's second word!

19:37.259 --> 19:38.802
Oh, my God!

19:38.803 --> 19:40.679
His second word was me!

19:40.680 --> 19:41.763
"Mommy."

19:41.764 --> 19:44.307
Oh, I love you, Stewie!

19:44.308 --> 19:46.727
Ooh, ooh. Say that again for Instagram.

19:51.232 --> 19:53.983
Well, well, I guess
he doesn't feel like it anymore.

19:53.984 --> 19:55.548
- Mommy!
- Ah!

19:55.549 --> 19:58.489
Say it again!
Say "Mommy" again for Instagram.

19:59.615 --> 20:01.255
All right.

20:01.256 --> 20:03.081
- I tried.
- Mommy!

20:03.082 --> 20:05.040
(BLEEP)!

20:10.793 --> 20:12.460
Wow, Stewie, kind of a big deal

20:12.461 --> 20:14.295
that your second word was "Mommy."

20:14.296 --> 20:16.214
Makes me think
you don't want to kill her

20:16.215 --> 20:18.091
and maybe you love her.

20:18.092 --> 20:20.176
No, no, no. No, no, no.

20:20.177 --> 20:22.345
No, no, that's what I <i>wanted</i> you
to think.

20:22.346 --> 20:23.763
- What are you talking about?
- Yeah.

20:23.764 --> 20:24.848
I scammed you, man.

20:24.849 --> 20:26.516
Took you for a ride, Jack.

20:26.517 --> 20:27.934
You thought you were a big wheel

20:27.935 --> 20:30.395
till you found out
squares don't roll, man.

20:30.396 --> 20:31.771
Dig this, hep cat.

20:31.772 --> 20:35.442
The Stew-man spun you round
like a Bill Evans 45.

20:35.443 --> 20:36.943
Wait, what's happening?

20:36.944 --> 20:38.445
I'll tell you what's happening, Brian.

20:38.446 --> 20:41.948
The whole family's becoming Jack
Kerouac's insufferable friends.

20:41.949 --> 20:44.784
No one wants us at
their apartment party, ya dig?

20:44.785 --> 20:47.620
Get hip to that, daddy,
or skit-scat out of the house.

20:52.126 --> 20:54.127
We don't know
how to end these shows anymore,

20:54.128 --> 20:55.963
so we just do nonsense.